A||||4||montage||35 or 40 profile problems?||||1||
Z||000000||montage||06-21-2001||10:36 AM||||I am planning on tire and wheel upgrades and would like to know if anyone has experienced problems with 35 or 40 series tires. We have some rough roads here and I would like to know if anyone has had problems with bent or cracked wheels using these tires. I am also having a problem locating the right wheels I would like 16X7.5 in front (or 17X7.5) and 17X8 (245 35 17) in the rear (88 formula) but am having a tough time finding both in the same wheel. I would like to use 225 (225 40 16 or 225 35 17) in the front and most 35 to 40 series tires require a 7.5" min rim width so would a 7" (easier to find) work?||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||06-21-2001||11:39 AM||||run a 235-40-17 on the back and a 205-50-16<P>i've got 17s 215-45 up front and 235-40 out back.. and had 245-40 and 215-40 on my SE and never ahd a problem.. i drove through ann arbor/flint/port huron/detriot in january on my current set up and it beat the hell out of m e but the cars fine.. you REALLY have to do somthing dumb to crack a wheel... i'm runnin 7" up front an 8" out back.. even with an 18 you'd still need a 225-40-18.. 35 series are for civcs and cars that aren't really driven hard.. more for show.. a 40 although only 5% more tire does make a big difference in ride quality and performance.<P> <A HREF="http://www.tires.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tires.com</A>  for wheels and such...  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">           <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||saleenfiero||06-21-2001||04:47 PM||||From my experience, 35 section 17" tires are hard to come by, and look stupid unless the car is lowered.  18" 35's are okay though, but then your prices jump/.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||06-21-2001||04:55 PM|||| <A HREF="http://powerdog.com/tiresize.cgi" TARGET=_blank>http://powerdog.com/tiresize.cgi</A> <P>this is a big help<P>I'm running 225/45/17's up front<BR>            235/45/17's rear<P>good for track use , hard to steer at low speeds , but bigger tires up front helped to combat understeer.<P>JM ||||reg||1
